Read signed audience-safe advice. Native resume rechecks current facts

Usage: chio recovery explain [OPTIONS] --endpoint <ENDPOINT> --capability <CAPABILITY> --workflow-id <WORKFLOW_ID>

Options:
      --endpoint <ENDPOINT>
          
      --capability <CAPABILITY>
          
      --workflow-id <WORKFLOW_ID>
          
      --json
          Short alias for `--format json`
      --receipt-db <RECEIPT_DB>
          Optional SQLite database path for durable receipt persistence
      --revocation-db <REVOCATION_DB>
          Optional SQLite database path for durable capability revocation persistence
      --authority-seed-file <AUTHORITY_SEED_FILE>
          Optional file path for a persistent capability-authority seed
      --authority-db <AUTHORITY_DB>
          Optional SQLite database path for shared capability-authority state
      --budget-db <BUDGET_DB>
          Optional SQLite database path for durable shared capability budget state
      --session-db <SESSION_DB>
          Optional SQLite database path for durable admission, trust authority, and remote MCP session state
      --control-url <CONTROL_URL>
          Optional shared trust-control service base URL
      --control-token <CONTROL_TOKEN>
          Bearer token used to authenticate to the shared trust-control service. Prefer `CHIO_CONTROL_TOKEN` env over the argv form so the bearer does not leak via `ps` / `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` [env: CHIO_CONTROL_TOKEN]
      --control-authority-public-key <CONTROL_AUTHORITY_PUBLIC_KEY>
          Exact current public key expected from a remote capability authority [env: CHIO_CONTROL_AUTHORITY_PUBLIC_KEY=]
      --control-authority-trusted-public-keys <CONTROL_AUTHORITY_TRUSTED_PUBLIC_KEYS>
          Additional historical public key expected in the remote authority trust set
  -h, --help
          Print help
